{
  "fixtureId": "go-json-v1",
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "producer": "backend/internal/features/jobs/application/draftjson",
  "notes": [
    "Literal canonical expectations for the restricted go-json-v1 encoder: default encoding/json.Marshal with HTML escaping left enabled and no trailing newline.",
    "Every expectedUtf8/expectedHex/expectedByteLength/expectedSha256 was authored before the encoder implementation and is never regenerated by the tests; the tests compare measured encoder output against these literals and also re-verify the literals against each other.",
    "B2 validates no rich draft grammar, decodes no raw JSON and claims no DTO fingerprint. Cases marked unit=rich-shaped document shape only.",
    "Integer fixture inputs are decoded with json.Decoder.UseNumber and converted through a bounded strconv.ParseInt (base 10, bitSize 64); the loader never produces a float64.",
    "No claim is made about raw duplicate keys, lone surrogate escapes or exponent number forms: those are not reachable through this fixture.",
    "This file is intentionally pure ASCII (non-ASCII content is written as \\uXXXX JSON escapes) so that the expected bytes are pinned by expectedHex.",
    "non_ascii_map_key_rejected documents the ASCII map-key precondition. Invalid UTF-8 and non-whitelisted Go types are covered by canonical_test.go because JSON cannot carry them."
  ],
  "cases": [
